    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.bracketed\n\n### Description\n\nThe one keymap pair I miss from `vim-unimpaired`, compared to `mini.bracketed` are `[<Space>` and `]<Space>` to add lines above and below the current line. I using this a lot and wondering if you open to accept a PR for this.\r\n\r\nFor clarity here is the corresponding documentation from vim-unimpaired:\r\n\r\n```\r\nLINE OPERATIONS                                 *unimpaired-lines*\r\n\r\n                                                *[<Space>*\r\n[<Space>                Add [count] blank lines above the cursor.\r\n\r\n                                                *]<Space>*\r\n]<Space>                Add [count] blank lines below the cursor.\r\n```",
    "closed_at": "2024-03-07T09:03:43Z",
